Let the module map generator read headers past MAX_PATH on Windows.

`module-map-generator` writes each header's size into the toolchain module map. It asks `_stat64` with the
path relative to the working directory. Windows resolves it to an absolute path, and past 260 characters
`_stat64` fails with ENOENT. A deep libc++ header such as
`__cxx03/__type_traits/is_trivially_lexicographically_comparable.h`, below an output directory with a
transition suffix, already reaches 263 characters on a CI agent.

On Windows, build the absolute `\\?\` path, or `\\?\UNC\` for a UNC path, and read the size with
`GetFileAttributesExW`. That form has no MAX_PATH limit. Clang itself already opens such paths, because LLVM
adds the prefix in its file APIs.
